    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "c6aba109de98e2414eac3e6ff9b4fce3",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"natural-frequencies-and-mode-shapes\">Natural frequencies and mode shapes</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We compute the natural frequencies solving the generalized eigenvalue problem</span>\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||[\\boldsymbol{k} \\boldsymbol{X} = \\omega^2 \\boldsymbol{m}\\boldsymbol{X},||]</marimo-tex><span class=\"paragraph\">using the <a href=\"https://scipy.org\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">SciPy</a> function <a href=\"https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy-1.18.0/reference/generated/scipy.linalg.eigh.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">scipy.linalg.eigh</a>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "9fe4ac736292477faafeeb3afd82dc6f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "a5d64468a642bfd008c186851f979d4b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"squares-of-the-natural-frequencies-rads2\">Squares of the natural frequencies (rad/s)\u00b2</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\omega_1^2 = 5.359||)</marimo-tex>, &nbsp; &nbsp;<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\omega_2^2 = 74.641||)</marimo-tex></span>\n<h3 id=\"natural-frequencies-rads\">Natural frequencies (rad/s)</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\omega_1 = 2.315||)</marimo-tex>, &nbsp; &nbsp;<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\omega_2 = 8.640||)</marimo-tex></span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "9d11cac0336c5b711fec9b164029e9c6",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"modal-shapes\">Modal shapes</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Modal shapes are normalized to norm 1.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X^{(1)} =||)</marimo-tex> <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\begin{bmatrix} -0.095 \\\\ -0.258 \\\\ \\end{bmatrix}||)</marimo-tex> &nbsp; &nbsp; <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(X^{(2)} =||)</marimo-tex> <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\begin{bmatrix} -0.353 \\\\ 0.258 \\\\ \\end{bmatrix}||)</marimo-tex> &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "439f26e2cf2e4c95647da8f33c07a3d9",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"graphical-representation\">Graphical representation</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Please understand that these shapes are drawn only to for a quick visual assessment of the relative magnitudes. These values may represent displacements, rotations or other degrees of freedom, and most likely aren't even in the same direction.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Remember also that the absolute magnitudes don't mean anything, any multiple of a mode shape is also a mode shape.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This can take a while to generate the animation. Be a little bit patient.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
